{"id":"14b822d4-a43e-4c1b-90e2-994df1794e70","object":"chat.completion","created":1784999577,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    threshold = case['threshold']\\n    calls = case['calls']\\n    accepted_ids = []\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    for call in calls:\\n        call_id = call['call_id']\\n        parseable = call['parseable']\\n        loss_without = call['loss_without_call']\\n        loss_with = call['loss_with_call']\\n        tokens = call['prediction_tokens']\\n        if tokens <= 0:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"prediction_tokens must be positive\\\")\\n        diff = loss_without - loss_with\\n        normalized_gain = diff / tokens\\n        normalized_gain_rounded = round(normalized_gain, 8)\\n        accepted = parseable and normalized_gain >= threshold\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accepted,\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": normalized_gain_rounded\\n        })\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_ids.append(call_id)\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\"}","reasoning_content":"We need to write Python code for solve(case) that processes the given case payload according to the task description. The task is about API call filtering: For each call, compute gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call. Then normalize gain by dividing by prediction_tokens (if prediction_tokens > 0, else maybe treat as zero? But from fixtures prediction_tokens are positive integers). Then check if parseable is true and normalized_gain >= threshold. If both, accept call. Return accepted_call_ids list of call_ids and diagnostics list of dicts with accepted bool, call_id, normalized_gain (rounded? The output schema says number, but we need to decide rounding. The candidate_artifact says \"rounded per-call di