ould treat as not accepted. But we should handle gracefully. I'll treat as normalized_gain = 0 if prediction_tokens <= 0 (or undefined). But better to raise ValueError? The spec says \"Raise ValueError for an infeasible or structurally invalid case\". If prediction_tokens is missing or non-positive, that might be invalid. The fixtures have positive ints. I'll assume positive.\n\nAlso threshold is given in case['threshold'].\n\nOutput: accepted_call_ids list of strings; diagnostics list of dicts with accepted bool, call_id string, normalized_gain number.\n\nWe need to return JSON object with these keys.\n\nNow write the solve function.\n\nImplementation details:\n- Extract threshold = case['threshold']\n- calls = case['calls']\n- Initialize accepted_ids = [], diagnostics = []\n- For each call in calls:\n    - call_id = call['call_id']\n    - parseable = call['parseable']\n    - loss_without = call['loss_without_call']\n    - loss_with = call['loss_with_call']\n    - tokens = call['prediction_tokens']\n    - Compute diff = loss_without - loss_with\n    - normalized_gain = diff / tokens if tokens > 0 else 0.0 (or maybe raise)\n    - accepted = parseable and normalized_gain >= threshold\n    - normalized_gain_rounded = round(normalized_gain, 8)  # adjust precision\n    - diagnostics.append({\"accepted\": accepted, \"call_id\": call_id, \"normalized_gain\": normalized_gain_rounded})\n    - if accepted: accepted_ids.append(call_id)\n- Return {\"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_ids, \"diagnostics\": diagnostics}\n\nCheck that diagnostics order matches calls order.\n\nNow produce the Python code as a string.\n\nThe entire response must be a JSON object with key \"implementation\" and value being the Python source string, properly escaped.\n\nWe need to output only that JSON object, no extra text.\n\nLet's write the code."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2171,"completion_tokens":1280,"total_tokens":3451,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens"